%description:

A deviation of StochasticChannelModel::computeShadowing() from the
specification, recorded rather than fixed: how a moving UE's shadowing is
correlated over the distance it travels.

TR 38.901 V16.1.0 clause 7.4.4, eq. (7.4-5), gives the normalized
autocorrelation of shadow fading over a horizontal displacement dx as

    R(dx) = exp(-dx / d_cor)

with d_cor the "correlation distance in the horizontal plane" of Table 7.5-6.
TR 36.873 clause 7.2.4 and TR 36.814 clause B.1.2.1.1 say the same, after
Gudmundson and ITU-R P.1816.

The model updates the value with the first-order recurrence

    att = a * old + sqrt(1 - a^2) * N(0, sigma)

which has exactly the autocorrelation R over a step dx if and only if
a = R(dx). The specification therefore fixes a = exp(-dx / d_cor), for every
displacement. The model deviates in two ways:

 - it uses a = exp(-0.5 * dx / d_cor), which doubles the correlation length;
 - it holds the value until the UE has moved more than d_cor, so the
   correlation is 1 below d_cor and the process is stepwise.

The checks below grade the specification's update against the draw the model
makes, replayed from an RngSnapshot, at displacements below and above d_cor.
ChannelModelShadowing pins what the model does today, so that any change to it
fails there by name. When the model follows the specification, update that pin
and drop the %expected-failure line here.

%expected-failure: the shadowing correlation is exp(-0.5*dx/d_cor) with a hold below d_cor, not TR 38.901's exp(-dx/d_cor)

%includes:
#include "SchedulerTestUtil.h"
#include "ChannelModelTestUtil.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;

%file: harness.ned
import simu5g.common.binder.Binder;
import simu5g.common.carrierAggregation.CarrierAggregation;
import simu5g.stack.phy.channelmodel.Tr38901ChannelModel;

network Harness
{
    submodules:
        binder: Binder;
        carrierAggregation: CarrierAggregation;
        bsChannelModel: Tr38901ChannelModel;
        test: Test;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = Harness
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = ""
sim-time-limit = 100s

*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 3.5GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 10
**.cellInfoModule = ""
*.binder.printTrafficGeneratorConfig = false

# Stated rather than inherited, as in ChannelModelShadowing. The LOS state is
# fixed, so that computeShadowing() draws nothing but the shadowing.
**.scenario = "URBAN_MACROCELL"
**.shadowing = true
**.correlationDistance = 50m
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = true

%no-default-inifile: 1

%activity:
Checker c;
auto *bs = harnessModule<StochasticChannelModel>(this, "bsChannelModel");
StubEndpoint bsEndpoint;
bs->setPhy(&bsEndpoint);
ChannelModelProbe bsProbe(bs);
PathLossModel *pathLoss = bsProbe.pathLoss();
const double dcorr = bs->par("correlationDistance").doubleValue();
const double d3D = 200.0, d2D = 198.6, speed = 10.0;
const double sigma = pathLoss->getShadowingStdDev(d3D, d2D, false);

// The specification's update of a value `old` over a displacement dx, with the
// normal deviate the model is about to draw.
auto specUpdate = [&](double old, double dx, RngSnapshot& snapshot) {
    double a = exp(-dx / dcorr);
    return a * old + sqrt(1 - a * a) * omnetpp::normal(snapshot.rng(), 0, sigma);
};

{
    // Below d_cor: 20 m at 10 m/s. R(20 m) = exp(-0.4) = 0.67, so the value is
    // correlated with the old one, not equal to it.
    const LinkKey key(MacNodeId(1200));
    bsProbe.losMap()[key] = false;
    double old = bs->computeShadowing(d3D, d2D, key, MacNodeId(1200), speed, false);
    wait(2.0);
    RngSnapshot snapshot(bs);
    double expected = specUpdate(old, 2.0 * speed, snapshot);
    double got = bs->computeShadowing(d3D, d2D, key, MacNodeId(1200), speed, false);
    c.expectNear("after 20 m (below d_cor = 50 m) the value follows a = exp(-dx/d_cor), not held",
            got, expected, 1e-12);
}
{
    // Above d_cor: 60 m at 10 m/s. R(60 m) = exp(-1.2) = 0.30.
    const LinkKey key(MacNodeId(1201));
    bsProbe.losMap()[key] = false;
    double old = bs->computeShadowing(d3D, d2D, key, MacNodeId(1201), speed, false);
    wait(6.0);
    RngSnapshot snapshot(bs);
    double expected = specUpdate(old, 6.0 * speed, snapshot);
    double got = bs->computeShadowing(d3D, d2D, key, MacNodeId(1201), speed, false);
    c.expectNear("after 60 m (above d_cor) the value follows a = exp(-dx/d_cor), not exp(-0.5*dx/d_cor)",
            got, expected, 1e-12);
}

c.summary();

%contains: stdout
modelchecks=2 modelfailures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
